            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": ">So what would happen if we use :cd？And i have to say, every if we merge it, it donn't implement the function we expect to see in #39239\r\n>\r\nIf you use `:cd` then it will restart using that directory, so that's unchanged. But this PR makes so that if you use `:bcd`, `:lcd`, etc then it will use the global CWD instead. I think it's a worthwhile change, since #39586 has been stalled for a long time.\r\n\r\n>dir.lua change the cwd of nvim?\r\n>\r\nIt changes the buffer-local directory.\r\n\r\nI don't really understand what the suggestion is regarding the libuv stuff.\r\n",
