            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Ok, I need to rearrange my expression.\r\n\r\n>Restart will transfer a buffer/tab/window local CWD to the new nvim's global CWD.\r\n\r\nFirst of all, this conclusion is wrong. Just look at the code path, `b_localdir` or sth never appear in the code path. So even if it really change the `cwd` it  use when restart after typing `:bcd` or sth, the path can't be related to `b_localdir` but only `cwd` of nvim process. Just check the callstack.\r\n\r\n> what if we hack in the 'channel...' func to see what path it use when 'dir=null'?\r\n\r\nWell, at that time, i thought the problem would be  inside `channel_job_start`, when `cwd==NULL`, we probably access the `b_localdir` or sth, so i want you to take a look to find out what it is. But now it's clear that it's just a coincidence that `pwd` equal to `b_localdir`, so you think it is `b_localdir` to blame.\r\n\r\n",
